    <node id="src.intellicrack.core.hexpat.data_reader.from_document">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">from_document</data>
      <data key="d5">['document']</data>
      <data key="d4">Create a DataReader from a HexDocument PyO3 object.

The document is expected to expose ``read(offset, length) -&gt; list[int]``
and ``length() -&gt; int`` methods as provided by the Rust/PyO3 binding.

Args:
    document: A HexDocument PyO3 object with ``read`` and ``length``
        methods.

Returns:
    DataReader: A DataReader backed by the supplied HexDocument.</data>
    </node>
