    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui._screen_compat">
      <data key="d0">module</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d2">D:\Intellicrack\src\intellicrack\ui\_screen_compat.py</data>
      <data key="d3">src.intellicrack.ui._screen_compat</data>
      <data key="d4">Screen geometry detection for PyQt6 SIP-generated bindings.

Provides wrapper functions that use dynamic attribute dispatch to access
Qt screen and widget geometry methods. These wrappers exist because
basedpyright cannot resolve certain inherited method signatures from
the auto-generated PyQt6 type definitions. Each function performs a real
runtime call to the underlying Qt method.

Every wrapper validates that the target method exists at runtime and
raises ``AttributeError`` with a clear diagn...</data>
    </node>
    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui._screen_compat._resolve">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">_resolve</data>
      <data key="d5">['obj', 'method_name']</data>
      <data key="d4">Resolve a method on a Qt object, raising a clear error if absent.

Args:
    obj: The Qt object instance.
    method_name: The camelCase method name to look up.

Returns:
    Callable[..., Any]: The bound method callable.

Raises:
    AttributeError: If the method does not exist on the object.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui._screen_compat.get_screen_geometry">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">get_screen_geometry</data>
      <data key="d5">['app']</data>
      <data key="d4">Return the primary screen's available area as (x, y, width, height).

Args:
    app: The QApplication instance.

Returns:
