    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui.panels.hex_tools_panel._demangle_msvc">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">_demangle_msvc</data>
      <data key="d5">['mangled']</data>
      <data key="d4">Attempt to demangle an MSVC-mangled symbol.

Handles the ``?name@scope1@scope2@@qualifiers`` pattern commonly
used by the MSVC linker.

Args:
    mangled: The mangled symbol string starting with ``?``.

Returns:
    str: Demangled representation, or the original if not parseable.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui.panels.hex_tools_panel._demangle_rust">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">_demangle_rust</data>
      <data key="d5">['mangled']</data>
      <data key="d4">Attempt to demangle a Rust-mangled symbol.

Handles legacy ``_ZN`` (length-prefixed path segments) and v0
``_R`` Rust symbol formats.

Args:
    mangled: The mangled symbol string starting with ``_ZN`` or ``_R``.

Returns:
    str: Demangled path, or the original if not parseable.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="src.intellicrack.ui.panels.hex_tools_panel._demangle_symbol">
      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">_demangle_symbol</data>
      <data key="d5">['mangled']</data>
      <data key="d4">Demangle a symbol using the appropriate strategy.

Tries cxxfilt first for Itanium/GCC mangling, then falls back to
MSVC (``?`` prefix) and Rust (``_ZN`` / ``_R`` prefix) parsers.

Args:
    mangled: The mangled symbol string.

Returns:
    str: Demangled symbol, or original if no strategy matched.</data>
    </node>
